//~ question: Does `linear` treat the two constructors of a disjunction's proofs as building different proofs?
//~ spec: proofs.procedures.linear
//~ rfc: 0005

// Any two proofs of one proposition are equal, so `left === right` is no contradiction.
logic fn absurd(
    left: @(True || True),
    right: @(True || True),
    t: @True,
    from_left: @(left === Or::Left @ t),
    from_right: @(right === Or::Right @ t),
    same: @(left === right),
) -> @False {
    linear((from_left, from_right, same)) //~ error: cannot prove `False` from the facts given: `Or::Left` and `Or::Right` build proofs, and the constructors of a proposition are neither injective nor distinct
}
